    "content='What is the maternity leave policy?' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='e76337af-4238-4158-9b5d-c5b1610c84ea'",
    "content='' additional_kwargs={'function_call': {'name': 'search_hr_policy', 'arguments': '{\"question\": \"maternity leave policy\"}'}, '__gemini_function_call_thought_signatures__': {'649eab21-9ae2-4297-989e-3b3fd4c117aa': ''}} response_metadata={'finish_reason': 'STOP', 'model_name': 'gemini-2.5-flash', 'safety_ratings': [], 'model_provider': 'google_genai'} id='lc_run--01a1638e-3c55-77d1-ba8a-2e9c10393bb4-0' tool_calls=[{'name': 'search_hr_policy', 'args': {'question': 'maternity leave policy'}, 'id': '649eab21-9ae2-4297-989e-3b3fd4c117aa', 'type': 'tool_call'}] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 384, 'output_tokens': 67, 'total_tokens': 451, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}, 'output_token_details': {'reasoning': 48}}",
    "content=\"[Source: maternity_paternity_policy.txt]\\nMATERNITY AND PATERNITY LEAVE POLICY\\r\\n\\r\\nPolicy Category: Maternity Paternity\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Purpose\\r\\nThis policy outlines paid leave entitlements for employees becoming parents through childbirth, surrogacy, or adoption.\\r\\n\\r\\n2. Maternity Leave\\n\\n[Source: maternity_paternity_policy.txt]\\n2. Maternity Leave\\r\\nEmployees who give birth are entitled to 26 weeks of paid maternity leave, which may begin up to 8 weeks before the expected delivery date. This entitlement applies to employees who have completed at least 80 days of service in the 12 months preceding the expected delivery date.\\r\\n\\r\\n3. Paternity Leave\\n\\n[Source: maternity_paternity_policy.txt]\\n8. Interaction With Other Leave\\r\\nMaternity, paternity, and adoption leave are separate from and do not reduce the employee's annual leave balance as described in the Leave Policy. Employees continue to accrue annual leave while on maternity, paternity, or adoption leave.\\r\\n\\r\\n9. Probationary Employees\\n\\n[Source: maternity_paternity_policy.txt]\\n6. Job Protection\\r\\nEmployees returning from maternity, paternity, or adoption leave are guaranteed reinstatement to the same role or an equivalent role with the same pay and seniority, in line with applicable local labor law.\\r\\n\\r\\n7. Phased Return to Work\\r\\nEmployees returning from maternity or adoption leave may request a phased return, working reduced hours for up to 4 weeks at full pay, subject to manager and HR approval.\\r\\n\\r\\n8. Interaction With Other Leave\\n\\n[Source: maternity_paternity_policy.txt]\\n9. Probationary Employees\\r\\nEmployees on probation (see the Probation Policy) who become eligible for maternity, paternity, or adoption leave during their probation period have their probation period paused and resumed upon return, rather than counted against them.\" name='search_hr_policy' id='c3843aa1-ee1a-4684-8dcc-2ff009605acd' tool_call_id='649eab21-9ae2-4297-989e-3b3fd4c117aa'",
    "content=[{'type': 'text', 'text': \"The maternity leave policy provides employees who give birth with 26 weeks of paid maternity leave. This leave can commence up to 8 weeks before the expected delivery date. To be eligible, employees must have completed at least 80 days of service in the 12 months preceding the expected delivery date.\\n\\nKey aspects of the policy include:\\n*   **Job Protection:** Employees returning from maternity leave are guaranteed reinstatement to the same or an equivalent role with the same pay and seniority, in accordance with local labor law.\\n*   **Phased Return to Work:** Employees may request a phased return, working reduced hours for up to 4 weeks at full pay, subject to manager and HR approval.\\n*   **Interaction with Other Leave:** Maternity leave is separate from and does not reduce an employee's annual leave balance. Employees continue to accrue annual leave while on maternity leave.\\n*   **Probationary Employees:** For employees on probation, the probation period is paused during maternity leave and resumes upon their return.\\n\\nThis information is sourced from the `maternity_paternity_policy.txt` document.\", 'extras': {'signature': ''}}] additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'finish_reason': 'STOP', 'model_name': 'gemini-2.5-flash', 'safety_ratings': [], 'model_provider': 'google_genai'} id='lc_run--01a1638e-639c-7a43-a873-bcaa931a74bd-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 853, 'output_tokens': 354, 'total_tokens': 1207, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}, 'output_token_details': {'reasoning': 126}}",
    "content='Does that apply during probation' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='5a02aef4-970d-44fc-8e41-5f41c2489484'",
    "content=[{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Yes, the maternity leave policy applies to probationary employees. If an employee on probation becomes eligible for maternity leave during their probation period, their probation period is paused and will resume upon their return from leave, rather than being counted against them. This information is from the `maternity_paternity_policy.txt` document.', 'extras': {'signature': ''}}] additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'finish_reason': 'STOP', 'model_name': 'gemini-2.5-flash', 'safety_ratings': [], 'model_provider': 'google_genai'} id='lc_run--01a1638e-a824-7e42-aaae-2b3fbdbe8408-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1038, 'output_tokens': 122, 'total_tokens': 1160, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}, 'output_token_details': {'reasoning': 57}}",
