    "content='[Source: work_from_home_policy.txt]\\nWORK FROM HOME POLICY\\r\\n\\r\\nPolicy Category: Work From Home\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Purpose\\r\\nThis policy outlines the eligibility, expectations, and process for employees working remotely on a regular or occasional basis.\\r\\n\\r\\n2. Eligibility\\r\\nEmployees who have completed their probation period (see the Probation Policy) and whose role does not require a fixed physical presence (e.g., front-desk, warehouse, or facilities roles) are eligible to work from home, subject to manager approval.\\n\\n[Source: reimbursement_policy.txt]\\n3. Home Office Setup Allowance\\r\\nEmployees eligible for the Work From Home Policy may claim a one-time home office setup allowance of up to 15,000 (local currency) within their first 3 months of eligibility, covering items such as a desk, chair, or monitor. Receipts are required for all claims.\\r\\n\\r\\n4. Internet and Mobile Reimbursement\\n\\n[Source: work_from_home_policy.txt]\\n3. Standard Work From Home Allowance\\r\\nEligible employees may work from home up to 2 days per week as a standing arrangement, agreed with their manager. Employees are not permitted to work from home every day as a default arrangement; teams are expected to maintain in-office collaboration on at least 3 days per week unless the role is designated fully remote in the employment contract.\\r\\n\\r\\n4. Occasional Work From Home\\n\\n[Source: work_from_home_policy.txt]\\n6. Equipment and Expenses\\r\\nThe company provides a laptop and any role-specific software required to work from home. A one-time home office setup allowance may be claimed through the Reimbursement Policy, subject to the limits defined there.\\r\\n\\r\\n7. Expectations While Working From Home\\n\\n[Source: work_from_home_policy.txt]\\n4. Occasional Work From Home\\r\\nIn addition to the standing 2-day allowance, employees may request occasional additional work-from-home days (e.g., for a home repair appointment or a focus-heavy task) by informing their manager at least 1 day in advance via chat or email. These occasional requests are not tracked formally but should be reasonable in frequency.\\r\\n\\r\\n5. Fully Remote Roles' name='search_hr_policy' id='fe8b1085-78e9-472d-82d5-3a3fa670832b' tool_call_id='74fc7ab5-2e49-41ea-8d57-4e5f8d923e83'",
    "content=[{'type': 'text', 'text': \"The Work From Home Policy outlines the eligibility, expectations, and process for employees working remotely.\\n\\nHere's a breakdown of the policy:\\n\\n**1. Eligibility:**\\n*   Employees must have completed their probation period.\\n*   Their role should not require a fixed physical presence (e.g., front-desk, warehouse, or facilities roles).\\n*   Eligibility is subject to manager approval.\\n\\n**2. Standard Work From Home Allowance:**\\n*   Eligible employees can work from home up to 2 days per week as a standing arrangement, agreed upon with their manager.\\n*   Employees are not permitted to work from home every day by default; teams are expected to maintain in-office collaboration on at least 3 days per week, unless the role is designated as fully remote in the employment contract.\\n\\n**3. Occasional Work From Home:**\\n*   In addition to the standard 2-day allowance, employees can request occasional additional work-from-home days (e.g., for a home repair appointment or a task requiring deep focus).\\n*   Such requests should be made by informing their manager at least 1 day in advance via chat or email.\\n*   These occasional requests are not formally tracked but should be reasonable in frequency.\\n\\n**4. Equipment and Expenses:**\\n*   The company provides a laptop and any role-specific software necessary for working from home.\\n*   **Home Office Setup Allowance:** Employees eligible for the Work From Home Policy may claim a one-time home office setup allowance of up to 15,000 (local currency) within their first 3 months of eligibility. This allowance covers items such as a desk, chair, or monitor, and receipts are required for all claims.\\n\\nThis information is primarily sourced from the `work_from_home_policy.txt` and `reimbursement_policy.txt` documents.\", 'extras': {'signature': ''}}] additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'finish_reason': 'STOP', 'model_name': 'gemini-2.5-flash', 'safety_ratings': [], 'model_provider': 'google_genai'} id='lc_run--01a16390-579a-7291-9d15-b386a5d40a80-0' tool_calls=[] invalid_tool_calls=[] usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1676, 'output_tokens': 475, 'total_tokens': 2151, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}, 'output_token_details': {'reasoning': 84}}"
  ]
}
